+# Runtime39: four-hop spatial FFT batching
+
+Isolated copy of frozen38. Only spatial_filter.py and raw_spatial_ring_bridge.py change at runtime. The filter is byte-identical to the already measured native proposed.py. Four 128-sample FFT windows are batched within each existing 512-sample bridge input block; OLA updates retain their original order. The bridge still emits one 4096-byte stereo float32 block per 512 input frames. The raw timing channel retains its 384-sample delay. Existing 128-sample process() and phase warmup remain unchanged.
+
+Eight local tests execute the actual original/new inner bridge loops with fake FIFO output and compare bytes, filter state, phase transition, diagnostic ON/OFF, partial input, and timing. Separately completed native NumPy evidence has nine exact cases and six timed children. Its approximately 27.6% pure-compute reduction applies only to that saved-input arithmetic test; it is not a whole-service CPU improvement or acceptance result. Native single-block traced peak allocation increased from 96,420 to 452,837 bytes; full-stack memory remains unmeasured.
+
+All calibration assets, phase code, worker, VAD thresholds, ASR, models, dialogue opener changes, FIFO transport and service lifecycle are byte-identical to38. Whisper Small/Piper3 remain unchanged. The prior 166 parent tests are inherited evidence, not newly rerun here. No C39 hardware/staging/adoption has occurred. Whole-stack CPU, memory and physical regression checks remain pending.
